# Streamlit Patterns (1.60+)

## Navigation (st.navigation + st.Page)

- Use `st.navigation` with `st.Page` API — not legacy `pages/` directory auto-discovery
- Use `app_pages/` directory (not `pages/`) for page modules
- `expanded` parameter accepts integer to control collapsed navigation items
- `st.Page` accepts external URLs
- Define pages: `st.Page("app_pages/chat.py", title="Chat", default=True)`

## Caching

- Use `@st.cache_data` for serializable values (DataFrames, lists)
- Use `@st.cache_resource` for global objects (models, DB connections)
- Always set `ttl` or `max_entries`
- Never cache without limits for user-specific data

## Performance

- Use `@st.fragment` for partial reruns (up to 80% faster)
- Use `st.form` to batch inputs
- Use conditional rendering with `st.toggle`, `st.segmented_control`, `@st.dialog`
- Avoid large DataFrames in `st.session_state`

## Data Handling

- Move aggregations to database level
- Prefer Parquet over CSV
- For 100M+ rows, use `@st.cache_resource`
- Sample or paginate before sending to browser
